  "appliesTo": "These are the recommended 'school term dates' set for schools in our area; some schools and academies may have different arrangements.",
  "academyNote": "Schools and academies may choose to adopt different term dates, and school training dates may vary - you must always check with your school to confirm term-time arrangements.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "York recommends that each school year starts on the first Monday in September and is 39 weeks long, giving 195 school days.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Dates are set using regionally agreed principles for Yorkshire and the North East, to help families who live, work or go to school in more than one council area.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "York prioritises keeping differences small with its immediate neighbours, North Yorkshire Council and East Riding of Yorkshire Council.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Each school sets its own training or inset days, which may change during the year.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "In 2026-27 the February half term is early (8 to 12 February 2027) and the summer term ends on Monday 26 July 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates/2"
    },
    {
      "fact": "After Christmas 2027 the spring term starts on Wednesday 5 January 2028, and the 2027-28 year ends on Wednesday 26 July 2028.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates/3"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2026-27 dates were last updated on 10 February 2025 and the 2027-28 dates on 26 February 2026.",
      "source": "https://www.york.gov.uk/attendance-truancy/school-term-dates/3"
    }
